al Hypercholesterolaemia (iSTART-FH): protocol for a randomised controlled trial","Authors":"Hayato Tada, Hirofumi Okada, Akihiro Nomura, Soichiro Usui, Kenji Sakata, Kenshi Hayashi, Noboru Fujino, Ayaka Yasugi, Shizuko Takahara, Yasuhito Imai, Masayuki Takamura, Masa-aki Kawashiri","Year":2021,"DOI":"10.1136/bmjopen-2021-053453","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"This study aims to test the hypothesis that AI-supported nutritional counselling is more effective in reducing LDL cholesterol than the in-person, face-to-face method in terms of improving LDL cholesterol control in patients with FH.This is a single-centre, unblinded, cross-over, randomised controlled study comparing the efficacy of AI-supported automated nutrition therapy with that of conventional human nutrition counselling in patients with FH.","Findings":"","Conclusions":"","Limitations":"","User_Notes":"yöntem makalesi  dyt karlılaştırması var  bulgular yayımlanmış mı bak  prompt yok, gerekli mi doğrula"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"p3swko","at":1774939556491}},"smart_blocks:Augmented Dietitian Okunmuşlar/tadaEffectsArtificialIntelligenceSsupporTed2021a.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.020485,0.0270861,-0.02024579,0.02631235,-0.01788903,-0.02497668,-0.01768484,0.04563453,0.00312651,-0.04984211,-0.01554303,-0.11734939,0.03413698,0.016249,0.03719743,-0.03068547,0.03111427,0.01080373,-0.04703365,0.0255313,0.05004991,-0.04189458,-0.00468668,-0.01933752,0.02032818,0.03138354,-0.00899819,-0.10670771,-0.06117791,-0.20441322,0.05812918,-0.05140849,0.04236004,-0.02614959,-0.03914097,0.0131507,-0.00631819,0.02746854,-0.02861148,0.01735623,0.0653998,0.00328608,0.03390149,0.00373762,0.02418737,-0.03746259,-0.03480411,-0.00195076,-0.03240604,-0.01574593,-0.05085639,0.01502655,0.04384802,0.03139629,0.02224259,0.02179256,0.052